note store/moving.om: the one answer of the addresses whose part the store build composes out while
note it moves to the new Interplane store (salvage, community, open, trending; store/mvsalvage.om,
note store/mvcommunity.om, store/mvopen.om, store/mvgrowth.om, composed by run.sh in place of
note server/no<part>.om when FORGE_STORE is set). Status 503 with no Retry-After (no time is promised),
note title "Moving" and the text "This part is moving to the new Interplane store and is not
note available yet." (server/pages.om ferrti, ferrmsg); a JSON request (a .json name, or Accept JSON)
note gets the forge/error/1 document with "reason":"moving" (server/jsonp.om fyerr). The request flag
note fmvng (server/util.om, reset by fresetr) is what tells those words apart from every other 503.
text tmvjs ".json"
note mvans: answer this request as moving; any method
fn mvans to long
put fmvng 0 1
put fretry 0 0
if mvjsnm
fyerr 503
end
ret 503
end
note mvjsnm: the path ends with ".json" (a JSON name needs no Accept header)
fn mvjsnm to bool
n = get fpathl 0
m = len tmvjs
if lt n m
ret false
end
for i ulong m
if ne get fpath add sub n m i get tmvjs i
ret false
end
end
ret true
end
note mvunder t: the path is t, or t then "/" and anything
fn mvunder t view uchar * to bool
if not fpre t
ret false
end
if eq get fpathl 0 len t
ret true
end
ret eq get fpath len t 47
end
